implementationPlan.description:
RED first, then the fix, in scripts/tests/daemon-autostart-argv.test.mjs only (load test-driven-development). Read mem:task-task-e5211efd8d6d47dd8d317cf43c619e67-handoff and mem:gotcha-plan-text-unicode-escapes-decoded first. The authoritative bytes are the planning prototype: reference diff /mnt/d/moe-scratch/e521-plan.x8b3/intended.diff (+39/-5 on e53f5a5c's file) and the finished file /mnt/d/moe-scratch/e521-plan.x8b3/scripts/tests/daemon-autostart-argv.test.mjs (sha256 ed65fb1aa576...). Applied verbatim on an unchanged base, your file hashes the same. Apply its hunks with the Edit tool (no git apply, cp or shell write: GLOBAL rail).
(0) RED: from the task worktree root, run checkRefs[0] once before any edit. It must exit 1 with `not ok 1` and `not ok 3` (the two 'literal-name paths' rows), `# tests 4`, and 'found 2' in the log.
(1) Selector. In the DRIVER template, replace the one-line `$calls = @($ast.FindAll({ ... $n.Extent.Text.Contains('--project') }, $true))` predicate with the diff's multi-line predicate:
- return $false unless the node is a CommandAst whose GetCommandName() is Start-Process;
- collect the call's VariableExpressionAst VariablePath.UserPath values and its StringConstantExpressionAst Value values with nested FindAll(..., $true);
- match only when the variables contain daemonScript AND the strings contain both start and --project.
PowerShell -contains is case-insensitive, like variable names. The check dispatch (~:9617) passes '--project' but has neither $daemonScript nor 'start'; the seat CLI (~:9467) passes no --project literal.
(2) Add `const AUTOSTART_COUNT = 'expected exactly one daemon-autostart Start-Process in moe-agent.ps1, found';` above DRIVER. Make the throw `throw "${AUTOSTART_COUNT} $($calls.Count)"`. That ${...} is deliberate JS interpolation into the PowerShell text: no other ${, no backtick and no backslash may appear inside the DRIVER template literal. Keep the exactly-one check (-ne 1) and everything after it unchanged.
(3) Comments. The DRIVER comment says why --project alone is not enough: the CQ-M07s check dispatch passes it too (task-e5211efd). The header comment gains the Row C sentence from the diff.
(4) Add plain() above `const show`: strip ANSI codes, join gutter-wrapped lines, collapse whitespace. It is copied from scripts/tests/subagent-mirror.test.mjs:18, proven on CI run 41830422144's wrapped pwsh 7 ConciseView text. Importing that file would run its tests.
(5) Add row C inside `for (const engine of ENGINES)`, after row B, reusing opts, fixtureRoot, run, show, PS_ARGS, childEnv and DRIVER_CAP_MS:
- read PS1 as utf8 and split on the newline character (this keeps the BOM and any CR);
- require exactly one line matching /\bStart-Process\b.*\$daemonScript\b/, with the count in the assert message;
- write cases.json as [] and the driver with the BOM spelled '\u{feff}' + DRIVER;
- for ['removed', 0, lines.toSpliced(at[0], 1)] and ['duplicated', 2, lines.toSpliced(at[0], 0, lines[at[0]])], write that copy into the fixture root, run the driver on it, and assert spawnError null, exit code not 0, and plain(r.stderr) includes `${AUTOSTART_COUNT} ${found}`;
- then call t.diagnostic(`autostart ${name}: ${AUTOSTART_COUNT} ${found}`), so the TAP log carries the mutant evidence the gate counts.
Error handling: every failure path is an assertion that prints show(r):
- a spawn error;
- a driver that accepts a mutant (exit 0);
- a driver that stops for another reason (a mutant that does not parse prints 'does not parse' and fails the message check);
- a hang (DRIVER_CAP_MS, 60 s, kills that recorded PID tree only);
- an anchor-line count other than 1 (moe-agent.ps1 changed shape).
Editing-tool trap, seen while planning: the Edit and Write tools turn a 4-hex-digit backslash-u escape into the raw character. Type the row C BOM exactly as '\u{feff}', and do not touch row A's existing BOM line: an old_string holding it cannot match. After editing, `grep -c $'\xef\xbb\xbf' scripts/tests/daemon-autostart-argv.test.mjs` must print 0, and `grep -cP '[^\x00-\x7e]' scripts/tests/daemon-autostart-argv.test.mjs` must print 4 (the é fixture lines, the same as at the base). Do not edit scripts/moe-agent.ps1 or .github/workflows/ci.yml.

Adversarial self-review of this task's diff (load adversarial-self-review), then the completion summary. Set `B=$(git rev-parse -q --verify MERGE_HEAD || git merge-base HEAD "$MOE_LAND_TARGET")` first.
(1) Scope. `git diff --stat "$B"` lists only scripts/tests/daemon-autostart-argv.test.mjs (about +39/-5). `git diff "$B" -- scripts/moe-agent.ps1 .github/workflows/ci.yml` is empty, so the autostart (~:1029) and the check-dispatch Start-Process (~:9617) are untouched (DoD 3). `git status --porcelain` shows no stray log, snapshot or mutant copy in the worktree: the gate log is under /tmp, and row C's copies live in each run's own mkdtemp root under %TEMP%, removed by t.after.
(2) Template literal. The only ${ inside DRIVER is ${AUTOSTART_COUNT}, with no backtick or backslash inside it. The predicate uses no PowerShell 7-only syntax (no ?:, ??, or && / || chains), so 5.1 parses it; the gate's 5.1 rows prove it.
(3) Byte traps. No raw U+FEFF (the grep from step 1 prints 0), and the non-ASCII line count is still 4.
(4) What could go wrong:
- two runs at once: each has its own fixture root;
- huge input: two 784 KB copies per engine, written and removed per run;
- a reformatted autostart call (multi-line, or single-quoted literals): the JS anchor or the AST selector fails loudly, never silently;
- CI's pwsh 7 ConciseView wraps at about 120 columns: the message is 77 characters, and plain() rejoins a wrap anyway;
- Linux node: all 6 rows skip with the existing reason (row C inherits opts), so `node --test scripts/tests/*.test.mjs` on Linux is unchanged.
(5) Optional, already run in planning: /mnt/d/moe-scratch/e521-plan.x8b3/mut.mjs applies one mutant to the test file of a scratch clone on D: (never the worktree): `node mut.mjs <clone> <your test file> <name>`. old-selector, no-exactly-one, pwsh-skipped and ps1-touched each turn the gate red. only-daemonScript (dropping the start/--project literals) stays green by design, because no other Start-Process runs $daemonScript.
In the summary, map each DoD item to its evidence:
- DoD 1: the gate's six ok rows and `# skipped 0`;
- DoD 2: row C's four diagnostics (removed: found 0; duplicated: found 2; per engine), plus the planning mutants;
- DoD 3: ps1diff=0 and the scope diff;
- DoD 4: secs=<n>.
